**Conversion from hospitalization level to patient level**

The original dataset is structured at the hospitalization level, meaning that each patient may have several hospitalization records. To create a patient-level dataset, we first retain only hospitalization stays that meet the inclusion criteria (inclusion_flag = TRUE). Then, for each patient, we select the earliest inclusion hospitalization according to inclusion_start. When several hospitalization records have the same earliest inclusion date, only one record is retained.

```{r}
# Convert the dataset from the hospitalization level to the patient level:
# keep only inclusion stays, then retain the earliest inclusion stay
# for each patient according to inclusion_start.
# If several stays have the same earliest date, keep only one of them.
df_patient <- df_large |>
  filter(inclusion_flag == TRUE) |>
  group_by(patient_id) |>
  slice_min(
    order_by = inclusion_start,
    n = 1,
    with_ties = FALSE
  ) |>
  ungroup()
```

